# ── Wine & Windows-app support ──
# wine (the metapackage) pulls in wine64 on amd64.
# wine32 requires lib32 multilib which bloats the ISO by ~500 MB;
# users who really need 32-bit Windows apps can `dpkg --add-architecture i386`
# post-install. We document this in the welcome screen.
# Bottles is not in Debian bookworm apt; it ships via Flathub, which
# our novau-store installs with one click.
wine
wine64
winetricks
fonts-wine

# ── Proton / Steam for gaming ──
# NOTE: steam-installer from apt depends on steam-libs-i386, which
# requires `dpkg --add-architecture i386` + the lib32 multiarch packages
# (~500 MB). Rather than bloating the ISO with 32-bit libraries that
# most users won't need, we ship Steam as a Flatpak (which bundles its
# own 32-bit runtime in a sandbox). Users install it via novau-store.
# Proton ships inside the Steam Flatpak automatically.
gamescope
mangohud
gamemode

